---
import '../styles/global.css';

const canonicalURL = 'https://www.dfsengineer.com/about/';

const personSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: 'Derek Jensen',
  url: canonicalURL,
  jobTitle: 'Founder, DFS Engineer Playbook',
  description:
    '20+ years in software development (backend, databases, web, mobile), now focused on AI and data analytics applied to NFL DFS.',
  worksFor: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'DFS Engineer Playbook' },
  mainEntityOfPage: { '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': canonicalURL },
};
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter+Tight:wght@500;600;700;800&family=Inter:wght@400;500&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" />
    <title>About Derek Jensen — DFS Engineer</title>
    <meta name="description" content="20+ years in software, now building NFL DFS projections and tools in the open. Why DFS Engineer Playbook exists, and what makes it different from a picks-selling service." />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalURL} />

    <meta property="og:type" content="profile" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="DFS Engineer" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="About Derek Jensen — DFS Engineer" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="20+ years in software, now building NFL DFS projections and tools in the open." />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonicalURL} />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="About Derek Jensen — DFS Engineer" />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="20+ years in software, now building NFL DFS projections and tools in the open." />

    <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(personSchema)} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <div class="wrap">
        <a class="wordmark" href="/">DFS<span>·</span>Engineer</a>
        <nav class="site-nav">
          <a href="/blog/">Blog</a>
          <a href="/about/">About</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="https://www.skool.com/brew-loyalty-6636">Join the community →</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">§ About</p>
        <h1>I'm Derek Jensen.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          20+ years building software. Now aiming all of it at NFL DFS —
          real models, real backtests, the math shown in the open.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="section-label">§ 01 — Why this exists</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          NFL DFS content is mostly a black box. You pay for someone's picks,
          or their gut feel dressed up as a service, and you have no real way
          to check their work.
        </p>
        <p class="lede">
          I got tired of that. I wanted tools and a process I could actually
          trust — because I could see how they worked, not because someone
          told me to trust them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="section-label">§ 02 — Where I'm coming from</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          I've spent 20+ years in software development — backend systems,
          databases, web apps, mobile apps, most of the stack at one point or
          another. The last several years have been focused specifically on
          AI and data analytics.
        </p>
        <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(160px,1fr)); gap:16px; margin-top:32px;">
          <div class="stat-card">
            <span class="stat-label">Years in software</span>
            <span class="stat-value">20+</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <span class="stat-label">Stack range</span>
            <span class="stat-value" style="font-size:20px;">Backend → Mobile</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <span class="stat-label">Current focus</span>
            <span class="stat-value" style="font-size:20px;">AI &amp; Data Analytics</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="section-label">§ 03 — Process, not picks</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          DFS Engineer Playbook is that experience pointed at one problem:
          building real NFL DFS projections, lineup tools, and a repeatable
          weekly process — for the rest of us, not just for people who can
          already build this stuff themselves.
        </p>
        <p class="lede">
          Everything here gets built the same way: state the model, run it
          against real results, show the work — good or bad. You can already
          see a piece of that on the homepage, where the projection numbers
          are backtested, not just asserted. I'm not selling picks. I'm
          building the tools and process I use myself, in the open.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="section-label">§ 04 — Follow the work</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Every model, every projection, every lineup decision gets written
          up as it happens. If you want a real process instead of a guess,
          start with the playbook — or join the community and follow along
          live.
        </p>
        <div style="display:flex; gap:16px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top:24px;">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/blog/">Read the playbook →</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="https://www.skool.com/brew-loyalty-6636">Join the community →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <div class="wrap">
        <a href="https://www.skool.com/brew-loyalty-6636">Join the DFS Engineer Playbook community →</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
